<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Image Tokenizer</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Results and Discussion ‣ 4 Experiments and Discussion ‣ OpenViGA: Video Generation for Automotive Driving Scenesby Streamlining and Fine-Tuning Open Source Models with Public Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows the results of fine-tuning the pre-trained <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">VQGAN</span> (TOK+DEC) using total loss <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{total}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Fine-Tuning the Tokenizer and Image Decoder ‣ 3.3 Our Streamlining and Fine-Tuning ‣ 3 OpenViGA ‣ OpenViGA: Video Generation for Automotive Driving Scenesby Streamlining and Fine-Tuning Open Source Models with Public Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and discriminator loss <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Fine-Tuning the Tokenizer and Image Decoder ‣ 3.3 Our Streamlining and Fine-Tuning ‣ 3 OpenViGA ‣ OpenViGA: Video Generation for Automotive Driving Scenesby Streamlining and Fine-Tuning Open Source Models with Public Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and explores the effects of individual loss components by omitting them (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-J</annotation></semantics></math>) during fine-tuning.
Although we employ a smaller tokenizer and partly different loss definitions, we start our investigations with the exact GAIA-1 loss weights <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>: <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\mathrm{L1}}\!=\!0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>L1</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\mathrm{L1}}\!=\!0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\mathrm{L2}}\!=\!2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>L2</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\mathrm{L2}}\!=\!2.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\prime}\!=\!0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\prime}\!=\!0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\mathrm{G}}\!=\!1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\mathrm{G}}\!=\!1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\mathrm{CB}}\!=\!1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>CB</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\mathrm{CB}}\!=\!1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\mathrm{SSL}}\!=\!0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>SSL</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\mathrm{SSL}}\!=\!0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Tokenizer<span id="S4.T3.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> and </span>image decoder discriminator and loss weight<span id="S4.T3.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> ablations: Quantitative results for using our <math id="S4.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{D}(\&gt;)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.220em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{D}(\&gt;)</annotation></semantics></math> with varying weights <math id="S4.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\mathrm{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\mathrm{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> for perceptual loss and generator loss during fine-tuning with the total loss <math id="S4.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{total}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Fine-Tuning the Tokenizer and Image Decoder ‣ 3.3 Our Streamlining and Fine-Tuning ‣ 3 OpenViGA ‣ OpenViGA: Video Generation for Automotive Driving Scenesby Streamlining and Fine-Tuning Open Source Models with Public Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), employing <math id="S4.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>(<a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Fine-Tuning the Tokenizer and Image Decoder ‣ 3.3 Our Streamlining and Fine-Tuning ‣ 3 OpenViGA ‣ OpenViGA: Video Generation for Automotive Driving Scenesby Streamlining and Fine-Tuning Open Source Models with Public Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) for discriminator training, with <math id="S4.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{SSL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>SSL</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{SSL}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Fine-Tuning the Tokenizer and Image Decoder ‣ 3.3 Our Streamlining and Fine-Tuning ‣ 3 OpenViGA ‣ OpenViGA: Video Generation for Automotive Driving Scenesby Streamlining and Fine-Tuning Open Source Models with Public Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) using <span id="S4.T3.8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DINOv1</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, evaluated on <math id="S4.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{BDDimg}}^{\mathrm{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>BDDimg</mi><mi>val</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{BDDimg}}^{\mathrm{val}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="S4.T3.8.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">VQGAN</span> models (TOK + DEC) were fine-tuned on <math id="S4.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{BDDimg/5s}}^{\mathrm{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>BDDimg</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></mrow><mi>train</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{BDDimg/5s}}^{\mathrm{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> for 200k iterations. Best results are in bold font, second best underlined. PSNR in (dB).
</span></span></figcaption>
