<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Omitting <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{SSL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>SSL</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{SSL}}</annotation></semantics></math> improves four metrics, but on the important perceptual FID and particularly CMMD it falls behind <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{total}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Removing the perceptual contribution <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{total}}</annotation></semantics></math> expectedly leads to catastrophic perceptual metrics, which are also not improved vs. <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{total}}</annotation></semantics></math> by omitting <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{L2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>L2</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{L2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to the strong PSNR, SSIM, MS-SSIM, one might be tempted to omit <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>G</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, but the price is again significantly worse perceptual metrics.
For all subsequent investigations, we adopt the total loss <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\mathrm{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\mathrm{total}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Fine-Tuning the Tokenizer and Image Decoder ‣ 3.3 Our Streamlining and Fine-Tuning ‣ 3 OpenViGA ‣ OpenViGA: Video Generation for Automotive Driving Scenesby Streamlining and Fine-Tuning Open Source Models with Public Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), as it overall yields best perceptual performance (LPIPS, FID, CMMD).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="S4.F5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15479v1/figures/vqgan_quali_files/quali_comp_zooms/v2/b1c9c847-3bda4659.jpg_og_with_RoI.jpg" id="S4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:685/685;" width="685" height="685" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering">a) Orig. image <math id="S4.F5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
