<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Conclusions</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduced OpenViGA, an open video generation system for automotive driving scenes.
Our method is build entirely on open-source pre-trained general-purpose models, which we fine-tune to the automotive domain using the public driving videos dataset BDD100K.
OpenViGA employs dedicated models for image tokenization, world modeling, and video decoding being able to generate coherent 256×256-sized videos frame-by-frame at 4 fps with a single frame algorithmic latency (lookahead).
We motivate design choices by quantitative and qualitative analysis, and
publish our training and inference code, thereby allowing for full reproducibility and deployment at academic scale.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
