<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="S4.F7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Generated videos<span id="S4.F7.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> using </span>OpenViGA<span id="S4.F7.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Each row shows a video generated with a different top-<math id="S4.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> sampling parameter, where <math id="S4.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,5,10,50,200,1000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,5,10,50,200,1000\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The first <math id="S4.F7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.128em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math> frames in each row represent the input frames from <math id="S4.F7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{BDDvid-4fps}}^{\mathrm{val-500}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>BDDvid</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>val</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{BDDvid-4fps}}^{\mathrm{val-500}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the other three frames represent the world model’s prediction after 1 (Frame 6), 2 (Frame 10), and 3 (Frame 14) seconds into the future, respectively. Note that input frames are transcoded using our TOK+DEC. Best viewed digitally with zoom.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
